<title>POLAND: Espebepe surges on speculative demand.</title>
<headline>Espebepe surges on speculative demand.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction firm Espebepe SA rose 9.3 percent to 4.1 zlotys in light trade due to speculative demand, as the company was experiencing financial problems, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's pure speculation -- investment funds have already gotten rid of their shares, so supply has decreased,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Espepebe, which has risen 32 percent from last month's low at 3.1 zlotys, made a net loss of 20.6 million zlotys over 1996's first 11 months.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
